  "description": "171 Esywn Road",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal constitutes development under the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, and the local planning authority is not satisfied that, based on the drawings submitted as part of the application, this proposal falls within any class of 'permitted development' specified within Schedule 2 to the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).\r\n\r\nINFORMATIVE: The proposed development fails to comply with Schedule 2 Part 1 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), 'Development within the curtilage of a dwellinghouse' as the ground floor enlargement would extend beyond the boundary of the curtilage of the dwellinghouse with the neighbouring proeprty, No.173. \r\n\r\nAdditionally, the development fails to comply with A.1 (j) (iii) of Class A and  B.1 (b) of Class B of Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) as (1) historic maps show a rear projection forming part of the original dwellinghouse and therefore the enlarged part of the dwellinghouse would extend beyond a wall forming a side elevation of the original dwellinghouse and have width greater than half the width of the original dwelling house.(2) The raised party walls would exceed the height of the highest part of the existing roof. "
  ],
